+<h2>Verification</h2>
+<p>Run the checks from the module directory:</p>
+<pre><code class="language-bash">cd flexpaxos
+go vet ./...
+go test ./... -count=1 -race -timeout=180s
+</code></pre>
+<p>Verified output:</p>
+<pre><code class="language-text">ok      example.com/flexpaxos   2.831s
+</code></pre>
+<p>The test suite covers:</p>
+<ul>
+<li><code>TestConfigValidation</code> and <code>TestLoadConfigBoundary</code>: legal configurations pass; <code>Q1+Q2 &lt;= N</code>, out-of-range quorums, unknown JSON fields, and trailing JSON are rejected.</li>
+<li><code>TestEveryLegalQuorumPairIntersects</code>: exhaustively enumerates every quorum subset for <code>N &lt;= 7</code> and proves there is no disjoint <code>Q1</code>/<code>Q2</code> pair for any config accepted by the loader.</li>
+<li><code>TestSafetyAllLegalQuorumsUnderReordering</code>: for every legal config with <code>N &lt;= 6</code>, 40 seeded schedules run two or three proposers with different values, independent random message delays, one proposer crash, and a conflicting recovery proposer. The harness records every commit and fails on the first time two different values are committed at index 0.</li>
+<li><code>TestRecoveryUsesOnlyPhase1Quorum</code>: crashes a proposer after it has sent phase-2 accepts but before it observes any phase-2 reply, so the value may already be chosen without the proposer knowing. A recovery proposer with a conflicting value must learn the old value from Q1 promises and commit it.</li>
+<li><code>TestStaleAcceptIsRejected</code>: an accept below the promised ballot is rejected; an idempotent duplicate prepare returns the durable accepted state.</li>
+</ul>
+<p>Operational note: in a real process, persist the acceptor state and the <code>BallotGen.last</code> value (or initialize the generator from the maximum ballot found on disk) before acknowledging messages. Leases may optimize the fast path, but a lease must never allow bypassing the ballot promise fence; otherwise an expired/stale leader can violate the same intersection argument.</p></div><div class='evidence'><h2>Evidence &amp; signatures</h2><pre># Evidence
