+<p>The failure class comes from treating an internal separator as “the first key of the right page” (or as a copied full key) instead of a value in the legal interval</p>
+<pre><code class="language-text">last_key(left) &lt; separator &lt;= first_key(right)
+</code></pre>
+<p>That causes several related failures:</p>
+<ol>
+<li><strong>No true suffix truncation</strong></li>
+<li>A separator that copies the entire right key is legal but not the shortest separator.</li>
+<li>
+<p>A truncated separator that is not strictly greater than the left page’s last key breaks routing and ordering.</p>
+</li>
+<li>
+<p><strong>All-equal-prefix split is mishandled</strong></p>
+</li>
+<li>If <code>leftLast</code> is a prefix of <code>rightFirst</code>, no proper prefix of <code>rightFirst</code> is greater than <code>leftLast</code>.</li>
+<li>The shortest legal separator is <code>leftLast + 0x00</code>.</li>
